    {
      "id": "ba545711a93fd1d5e0258b943abe725f7623da1d",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1078841824,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The issue with commenting that check out is that it's needed for retransmissions of segments that were *not* part of a multisegment PDU.\n\nTCP segments that are in order and not part of a subdissector PDU split across multiple frames don't get stored in the reassembly tables or elsewhere, which saves memory. When they're add to the reassembly tables, then the reassembly process (plus checking for `reassembled_in`, etc.) means that the subdissector isn't called a second time.\n\nBut as a result, if that check isn't there, then retransmitted segments that aren't part of reassemblies get sent to subdissectors a second time. That's wrong for most dissectors, and particularly bad for state based dissectors (HTTP, SMTP, etc.) If the TCP analysis stored the information that the desegmentation needed, that would be one way to help with reassembly. (I suppose the number of states could be increased; there could be a \"retransmission from the sender's perspective but also something that isn't present in the capture file yet.)\n\nNow granted, that check doesn't work for \"retransmissions that have additional data\" (#13523) as it is, unless there's yet another state added for that type.\n\nAnother approach, I suppose, would with out-of-order handling on to say that any segment that doesn't advance the maximum seen next seq number and is *not* part of a reassembly is something that shouldn't be passed to the subdissector. However, we'd still have to store that state for subsequent passes, and it really seems to be duplicating some of the TCP analysis work.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-08-26T05:26:51.082Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-08-26T06:40:16.177Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 168194289,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
