          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7543,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1078886700,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I fully agree with your comment, the commented part was there only as a test, with keeping in mind !2445 that would allow jumping over it.\nWhen putting back in place the comment and applying !2445 (through the Preference dialog and not by the right-clic) we can select all Retransmissions and force them as OOO in one action only. See :\n\nselect Retransmissions and force interpretation :\n![13388_with_2445_step1](/uploads/3b3f9fbc207f5d60297ebd1efd9e0788/13388_with_2445_step1.JPG)\n\nresult :\n![13388_with_2445_step2](/uploads/2c507fdd182d231311b3bfaaf07e2ab1/13388_with_2445_step2.JPG)\n\nThe other part of your comment, also, I agree. In fact one day we are probably going to consider different Retransmissions as a GUI information for the user, and Retransmissions as indications of what needs to be really processed internally by the program. In that latter case, some packets would be ignored, some would be taken into account. Until now my method was targetting the issues one by one, as considering the totality of the code before doing anything is a too big step if I'm not doing that as a full time activity. However, the lesson learned from different tickets is that things are converging in some way and we finally see that need to think about working on Retransmissions.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6797213,
            "username": "eugene.adell",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Eugène Adell",
            "state": "active",
